{"name":"Stone Mill","hex":"#b6b7ad","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stone","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard earthen substance that can form rocks; especially, such substance when regarded as a building material.","A piece of such material: a block of stone, rock or a pebble."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Constructed of stone.","Having the appearance of stone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stone"},{"term":"mill","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grinding apparatus for substances such as grains, seeds, etc. (Some are small and simple, and some are large and complex.)","The building housing such a grinding apparatus; also, any similar building that houses a similarly material activity (such as weaving, fulling, dying, etc.); the place of business comprising such a building and its outbuildings and grounds."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To grind or otherwise process in a mill or other machine.","To shape, polish, dress or finish using a machine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lebanon Township, New Jersey","blocks":[{"text":"Lebanon Township is the northernmost township in Hunterdon County, in the U.S. state of New Jersey. As of the 2020 United States census, the township's population was 6,195, a decrease of 393 (−6.0%) from the 2010 census count of 6,588, which in turn reflected an increase of 772 (+13.3%) from the 5,816 counted in the 2000 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/57_Musconetcong_River_Road%2C_New_Hampton%2C_NJ_-_looking_north.jpg/330px-57_Musconetcong_River_Road%2C_New_Hampton%2C_NJ_-_looking_north.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lebanon_Township%2C_New_Jersey"},{"title":"Stone Mill (Middlebury, Vermont)","blocks":[{"text":"The Frog Hollow Stone Mill, or as it is now referred to, The Stone Mill, is a historic industrial building at 3 Mill Street in Middlebury, Vermont. Built in 1840, it is an important local reminder of the town's industrial past, and was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1973. It presently houses a restaurant, a public market, event space and four hotel rooms as part of an extensive renovation conducted in 2019."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/06/Stonemill_2023.jpg/330px-Stonemill_2023.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stone_Mill_(Middlebury%2C_Vermont)"},{"title":"Millstone","blocks":[{"text":"Millstones or mill stones are stones used in gristmills, used for triturating, crushing or, more specifically, grinding wheat or other grains. They are sometimes referred to as grindstones or grinding stones."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Millstone_Anatomy.jpg/330px-Millstone_Anatomy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Millstone"},{"title":"Rock (geology)","blocks":[{"text":"In geology, a rock is any naturally occurring solid mass or aggregate of minerals or mineraloid matter. It is categorized by the minerals included, its chemical composition, and the way in which it is formed. Rocks form the Earth's outer solid layer, the crust, and most of its interior, except for the liquid outer core and pockets of magma in the asthenosphere. The study of rocks involves multiple subdisciplines of geology, including petrology and mineralogy. It may be limited to rocks found on Earth, or it may include planetary geology that studies the rocks of other celestial objects."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg/330px-Marsh_Butte_and_Geikie_Peak%2C_Grand_Canyon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rock_(geology)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/35/Lebanon_Twp_Seal.png/120px-Lebanon_Twp_Seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/35/Lebanon_Twp_Seal.png/250px-Lebanon_Twp_Seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/35/Lebanon_Twp_Seal.png/120px-Lebanon_Twp_Seal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALebanon_Twp_Seal.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lebanon_twp_019_nj.png/500px-Lebanon_twp_019_nj.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Lebanon_twp_019_nj.png/500px-Lebanon_twp_019_nj.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALebanon_twp_019_nj.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2013-05-06_17_29_22_Stream_and_forest_along_Turkey_Top_Road_in_northern_Lebanon_Township_in_Hunterdon_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg/500px-2013-05-06_17_29_22_Stream_and_forest_along_Turkey_Top_Road_in_northern_Lebanon_Township_in_Hunterdon_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2013-05-06_17_29_22_Stream_and_forest_along_Turkey_Top_Road_in_northern_Lebanon_Township_in_Hunterdon_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg/1280px-2013-05-06_17_29_22_Stream_and_forest_along_Turkey_Top_Road_in_northern_Lebanon_Township_in_Hunterdon_County%2C_New_Jersey.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/2013-05-06_17_29_22_Stre